    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d245-a1">

                <pb facs="0524" n="428" sameAs="frus:frus1874/pg428"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 603.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Norris to Mr.
                            Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Executive Chamber, Harrisburgh, Pa.</hi></placeName>,<lb/><date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1873-03-07"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >March</hi> 7, 1873</date>. (Received March 10.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In reply to your letter of the 3d instant,
                    making inquiry “whether the Philadelphia University of Medicine and Surgery have
                    authority to grant a diploma of Doctor of Philosophy to a person who has not
                    been a regular student of the university or who has not graduated in its course
                    of study,” by direction of the governor I have the honor to transmit herewith a
                    communication, with an accompanying circular from the secretary and treasurer of
                    the board of trustees of the University of Pennsylvania, “which doubtless convey
                    the information desired.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>A. WILSON NORRIS,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Private
                            Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hamilton Fish</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
